10:T70c,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Where do the $90K–$180K numbers come from?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Base salary ranges for marketing/creative roles plus standard loading: benefits, insurance, and payroll taxes (typically 25–35% on base), software, recruiting, and management time. Run your own market's numbers in the calculator on our homepage, the conclusion usually survives local adjustment."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is the monthly fee really fixed?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, each package is a flat monthly fee for a defined output level. If your needs grow (more properties, heavier seasons), you change tiers; nothing meters per asset behind your back."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What's the catch versus an in-house hire?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"An in-house person can walk the property daily and shoot spontaneously; we work from the assets your team sends. In practice clients find that trade easy, phone photos from staff plus our finishing covers it, but it's the honest difference."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do we have to commit to a long contract to get the savings?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No long lock-in is required to start. Begin with the free trial, then a monthly package, and ask us about commitment terms directly during the trial. Scale up, down, or pause as your season demands."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does this replace our whole marketing function?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No, it replaces the creative production layer: the design, video, and caption work that eats the most time. Strategy, paid media buying, and PR stay with whoever owns them now; our content plugs into their plans."}}]}5:["$","script","1",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$10"}}]
